From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:46:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: ring host ready early, and only once,
 on the BCM4389

Broadcom's driver rings the host-ready doorbell (DB1) right after the
common rings are set up and before it posts any buffer (bcmdhd
dhd_msgbuf.c dhd_prot_init(), hostrdy_after_init set in
dhd_pcie.c dhdpcie_bus_attach()). brcmfmac rings it only in preinit,
after the rx and control buffers are already posted. For the BCM4389,
which is told in host_cap that host ready will come, ring it once the
interrupt is set up as well.

With the PCIe debug level on, log the host-ready doorbell.

Broadcom's driver rings it only once, and brcmfmac's preinit must not
ring it a second time: the 20.101.90 firmware dies on that, with its
console showing

  THREADX TRAP INFO: Thread: main_thread ...
  TRAP 4(326dc8): pc 27489a, lr 27488d, sp 327020 ...  dfsr 80f, dfar 0

and the firmware's symbol map puts pc/lr in _hnd_die, with
pciedev_handle_hostready_intr+0x75 (0x2315f1) and pciedev_dpc on the
stack: a deliberate stop in the host-ready handler, 20 ms after the
second doorbell.

So skip the preinit host ready for the BCM4389, and write the value
Broadcom's driver writes (0x12345678, dhd_bus_hostready()).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c        | 25 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 8235c50a1..bb45ab252 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -1156,9 +1156,16 @@ static void brcmf_pcie_intr_enable(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo)
 
 static void brcmf_pcie_hostready(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo)
 {
-	if (devinfo->shared.flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_HOSTRDY_DB1)
+	if (devinfo->shared.flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_HOSTRDY_DB1) {
+		brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "host ready on 0x%x\n",
+			  devinfo->reginfo->h2d_mailbox_1);
+		/* bcmdhd dhd_bus_hostready() writes this value */
 		brcmf_pcie_write_reg32(devinfo,
-				       devinfo->reginfo->h2d_mailbox_1, 1);
+				       devinfo->reginfo->h2d_mailbox_1,
+				       devinfo->pdev->device ==
+				       BRCM_PCIE_4389_DEVICE_ID ?
+				       0x12345678 : 1);
+	}
 }
 
 static irqreturn_t brcmf_pcie_quick_check_isr(int irq, void *arg)
@@ -1731,7 +1738,12 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_preinit(struct device *dev)
 	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Enter\n");
 
 	brcmf_pcie_intr_enable(buspub->devinfo);
-	brcmf_pcie_hostready(buspub->devinfo);
+	/* The BCM4389 was told host ready right after its rings were set
+	 * up; its firmware traps on a second one (_hnd_die from
+	 * pciedev_handle_hostready_intr), so ring it only once.
+	 */
+	if (buspub->devinfo->pdev->device != BRCM_PCIE_4389_DEVICE_ID)
+		brcmf_pcie_hostready(buspub->devinfo);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -2506,6 +2518,13 @@ static void brcmf_pcie_setup(struct device *dev, int ret,
 	if (ret)
 		goto fail;
 
+	/* Broadcom's driver rings host ready as soon as the common rings
+	 * are set up, before it posts any buffer (bcmdhd dhd_prot_init(),
+	 * hostrdy_after_init), and the BCM4389 was told so in host_cap.
+	 */
+	if (devinfo->pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4389_DEVICE_ID)
+		brcmf_pcie_hostready(devinfo);
+
 	/* hook the commonrings in the bus structure. */
 	for (i = 0; i < BRCMF_NROF_COMMON_MSGRINGS; i++)
 		bus->msgbuf->commonrings[i] =
